    "text": "<p>For a cell, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><menclose notation=\"right\"><mi>Cu</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></menclose><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced close=\"\"><mrow><menclose notation=\"right\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></menclose><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi>Ag</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math>the cell potential is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>43</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The magnitude of standard electrode potential for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>|</mo><mi>Cu</mi></math> is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Given</mi><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Ag</mi></mrow><mi>&#920;</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>80</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
